## 13. Gate P6 Acceptance Criteria

Gate P6 may be marked PASS only when all of the following are true:

1. P5 projection/delta publication and error behavior are implemented and verified in the production renderer path.
2. Every selectable entry point uses one `SceneSelection`; raw node-index selection and dual legacy/editor mutation branches are removed from the P6 path.
3. Six selection kinds, idempotent event rules, explicit same-Primitive toggle, Escape, mutation fallback, and one end-of-frame revision are covered by CPU/UI tests.
4. A Primitive selection identifies a scene render occurrence, not merely a mesh primitive definition or mutable draw index.
5. Picks complete across frames without normal-path device idle waits; every request terminates and serial ordering prevents state reversal.
6. All authority/revision/scene-epoch/projection/device/viewport/view fence mismatch tests pass with no effect.
7. Current-fence blank/invalid/hidden and post-submit hidden/deleted/stale partitions have the explicitly specified single-versus-double behavior.
8. Single timeout, double exclusivity, drag suppression, same-Primitive clear, blank clear, and the strict timeout boundary pass under a fake clock.
9. Double hit produces exact finite camera center and speed, while double miss/stale does not touch camera or selection.
10. Browser focus expands/scrolls without forcing an active-tab change.
11. Node highlights exactly its visible subtree occurrences; Primitive highlights exactly its target occurrence; Inspector, Browser, and screenshot agree.
12. Logical-to-pixel conversion passes high-DPI, resize, edge, and backend surface-transform tests without double scaling.
13. Modal/gizmo/ImGui/pick/camera priority and R16 Escape/release partitions pass; each input event has at most one consumer, and the R16/O06 history contradiction has first been reconciled in the locked artifacts.
14. Clipboard Copy/parse/range/cross-document/overflow/no-history partitions pass D16 and the locked reference UI semantics.
15. Public include/link scans and build metadata prove only upstream Dear ImGui plus MGIF-owned adapters are used; no forbidden reference framework/helper dependency is introduced.

On the audited snapshot, items 1-15 are unverified or missing. The correct gate status is **NOT EVALUATED / NOT PASS**, not partial PASS.

## 14. Dependency Boundary

Allowed:

- Upstream Dear ImGui only in MGIF app/UI adapters, including OS clipboard access and input capture state.
- Existing MGIF `scene/editor`, `render`, `rhi`, app, math, and standard-library facilities.
- MGIF-owned backend-neutral interfaces and fake implementations for tests.

Forbidden:

- `nvcore`, `nvpro_core`, `nvapp`, `nvgui`, `nvvk`, any `nvvk*` variant, `nvvkgltf`, and any copied/linked reference helper API.
- Reference `SceneSelection`, `UiMouseState`, camera manipulator, ray picker, ObjectID helper, application framework, or renderer wrapper as a dependency.
- Public editor headers containing `Vk*`, `ID3D12*`, `ImTextureID`, reference namespaces, renderer dense indices, or raw reference render-node IDs.

Behavior may be clean-room reimplemented from the locked evidence. Source file names and helper architecture are not an API license.

